<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/harness/abide/measure',
        '/harness/preload',
        '/harness/gate/at-most',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/testPreload.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a test under the preload imports a .abide and a handler file of the app, and signs in — 38.109, 38.120'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/testPreload.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a test mounts a component, clicks it and reads the work the click did — 38.119'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Mount and measure components in the app's tests">
        <p>Add the line to the app's <code>bunfig.toml</code>. It registers a DOM with the
            counters installed, then builds the app so a test imports its <code>.abide</code>
            files as modules.</p>
        <Code language="toml" caption="server" code={`
            [test]
            root = "src"
            preload = ["@abide/harness/abide/preload"]
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Import a component straight into a test">
        <p>Under the preload a <code>.abide</code> file imports like any module.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="shared" code={`
            import { mount } from '@abide/harness/abide'
            import ProfileSummary from './ProfileSummary.abide'

            test('the initials show', async () => {
                using _summary = await mount(ProfileSummary({}))
                expect(document.querySelector('strong')?.textContent).toBe('AL')
            })
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
